# CUBE script: Level cap (OFF)
#
# ON means the level caps are active (a set cap flag limits the level); OFF means there is no level limit at all.
#
# What it does
#   Turns the level cap off: your Pokemon can level up without a limit, whatever the cap flags say.
#   The 10 caps stay in the ROM, for the next time.
#
# How to undo
#   Run CUBE_LevelCap_ON.hma, or press Ctrl+Z before you save.
#
# How to use
#   1. Open your CUBE ROM in HexManiacAdvance.
#   2. Drag this file onto HexManiacAdvance.
#   3. Look at the result, then save the ROM.
#   It works on every CUBE ROM from round 14 on, also on one that you changed and saved with an older .toml.
#   On any other ROM the script stops with a message and changes nothing.
#
# What it writes
#   One byte of the table cube.scripts.config (byte 5 = 0 for off). Nothing else in the ROM changes.
#
.python
tab = editor.SelectedTab
if tab.Model.GetAddressFromAnchor(tab.CurrentChange, -1, 'cube.scripts.config') < 0:
  tab.RaiseError('No CUBE script table (cube.scripts.config): this is not a CUBE ROM, or it is a CUBE older than round 14 (older Apply CUBE). Nothing was changed.')
  tab.AbortScript()
.end

@cube.scripts.config+5 0

.python
editor.SelectedTab.RaiseMessage('CUBE: level caps are now off.')
.end
